1
00:11:26,666 --> 00:11:32,666
The Hits Just Keep on Coming

2
00:22:53,333 --> 00:22:59,333
Narco Cultura is a crime, documentary film directed by Shaul Schwarz.

3
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:26,000
To a growing number of Mexicans and Latinos in the Americas, narco-traffickers
have become iconic outlaws and the new models of fame and success.

4
00:45:46,666 --> 00:45:52,666
They represent a pathway out of the ghetto, nurturing a new
American dream fueled by the war on drugs.

5
00:57:13,333 --> 00:57:19,333
Narco Cultura looks at this explosive phenomenon from within, exposing cycles of addiction to money,
drugs, and violence that are rapidly gaining strength on both sides of the U.S.-Mexico border

6
01:08:40,000 --> 01:08:46,000
Narco Cultura is a 2013 documentary film about the Mexican drug
war in Ciudad Juárez, directed by Shaul Schwarz.

7
01:20:06,666 --> 01:20:12,666
The two main focal points of the movie are Edgar Quintero of the narcocorrido
band Buknas de Culiacán and crime-scene investigator Richi Soto.

8
01:31:33,333 --> 01:31:39,333
The film explores themes of war on drugs, gang violence, mexican cartel.
